 "stimulus_html": "<figure id=\"fig2_4\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/1e9e33b33793d5c6.png\" alt=\"A Chinese man sits on a box labeled Order outside the closed Golden Gate of Liberty. His elbow is on his knee with his hand propping up his head. On the wall beside the gate is a sign that reads Notice—Communist Nihilist—Socialist Fenian and Hoodlum Welcome but No Admittance to Chinamen. Beside the man are bags labeled Industry, Peace, Sobriety. Behind the wall is an American flag. The caption at the bottom of the cartoon reads “The only one barred out. Enlightened American Statesman says ‘We must draw the line somewhere, you know.’”\">\n<figcaption>The text below image reads: “The only one barred out. Enlightened American statesman – ‘We must draw the line somewhere, you know.’”</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p><i>Refer to the image provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 615709,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "This political cartoon was primarily a response to",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1170804,
     "content_html": "the Red Scare"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170805,
     "content_html": "anti-Asian nativism"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170803,
     "content_html": "growing industrialization"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170802,
     "content_html": "the Open-Door policy"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615710,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The issues addressed in the political cartoon are similar to which issue from the first half of the nineteenth century?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1170808,
     "content_html": "The debate over Manifest Destiny"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170807,
     "content_html": "The “spot resolutions” and the argument against the Mexican War"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170809,
     "content_html": "Attitudes toward Irish immigrants"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170806,
     "content_html": "The “Corrupt Bargain”"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615711,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "On the basis of the ideas presented in the cartoon, the cartoonist would most likely agree with which of the following statements?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1170813,
     "content_html": "“The Chinese in this country have been for the most part peaceable and industrious.”"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170812,
     "content_html": "“California must be all American or all Chinese. We are resolved that it shall be American.”"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170811,
     "content_html": "“If we continue to permit the introduction of this strange people, with their peculiar civilization . . . what is to be the effect upon the American people. . . ?”"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170810,
     "content_html": "“The Chinese are a parasitic group of immigrants whose labor we should exploit.”"
    }
   ],
